module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalTypesDenseSubsitePullback
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalTypesSitePresentedPullback
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.RingedToposEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.RingedToposPullbackModulesComp
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.RingedToposTwoMorphismModules
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Topos.RingedToposReplacement
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Local types of modules are preserved by the pullback along a morphism of ringed topoi

Stacks 03DO asserts that the first seven of the eight local conditions of Stacks 03DL on a sheaf
of modules are stable under the pullback of Stacks 03D6 along an arbitrary morphism of ringed
topoi.  This file
proves the four clauses 03DL (1), (2), (3) and (6) — locally free, finite locally free, locally
generated by sections, and quasi-coherent — at that generality, by the source's own route: the
morphism is factored by Stacks 03CR as

```
(Sh(C), O_C)   --(g, g♯)-->   (Sh(C'), O_{C'})
     |                               |
  (f, f♯)                        (h, h♯)
     |                               |
     v                               v
(Sh(D), O_D)   --(e, e♯)-->   (Sh(D'), O_{D'})
```

whose two vertical arrows are the equivalences attached to dense subsite inclusions and whose
bottom arrow comes from a left exact morphism of sites, and the clause is carried around the
square.

Three of the four sides are already available: along `e` and `g` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules_ofDenseSubsite` and its
companions, and along `h` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules_of_isMorphismOfSites` and
its companions.  What this file adds is the lift of a sheaf of modules *back* across a dense
subsite inclusion — the clause is a hypothesis on a module on `(Sh(D), O_D)`, whereas what the
square consumes is a module on `(Sh(D'), O_{D'})` — and the assembly.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.denseSubsiteLift`: **a sheaf of modules on a dense subsite
  is the pullback of one on the ambient site**, namely of the one that the restriction of
  modules sends to it once the two restrictions of scalars are undone.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesObjDenseSubsiteLiftIso`: the identification
  of the pullback of that module with the given one.

The lift carries five of the clauses of Stacks 03DL, (1), (2), (3), (6) and (8); the coherent
one, `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isCoherentOnSite_denseSubsiteLift`, is consumed not here
but by the one-sided factorization in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.CoherentPullbackUnderEquivalence`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules`: **Stacks 03DO for the
  clause 03DL (1)**, for an arbitrary morphism of ringed topoi.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules`: **Stacks 03DO
  for the clause 03DL (2)**.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_pullbackModules`:
  **Stacks 03DO for the clause 03DL (3)**.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isQuasicoherentOnSite_pullbackModules`: **Stacks 03DO for
  the clause 03DL (6)**.

## Implementation notes

**The lift is built from forward transports only.**  The pullback along a dense subsite
inclusion is the restriction of modules followed by two restrictions of scalars along
isomorphisms of sheaves of rings; the module on the ambient site attached to `F` is obtained by
restricting the scalars of `F` along the two inverse isomorphisms and then applying the
quasi-inverse of the restriction of modules, which is an equivalence by the Comparison Lemma.
Each clause therefore travels to the lift by two applications of its invariance under
restriction of scalars along an isomorphism of sheaves of rings and one application of
Stacks 03DM, all in the direction in which those statements are proved; no reflection statement
is needed.

**The square is consumed up to 2-isomorphism.**  Stacks 03CR asserts that the square commutes in
the sense of a 2-isomorphism of the two composites, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.TwoIso.pullbackModulesIso` turns that into an isomorphism of
the two pullbacks of sheaves of modules; the two composites are split by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesCompIso`, the pseudo-functoriality of
Stacks 03D8.

**No hypotheses on the sites.**  The two ringed topoi are `RingedTopos.{w, w, w}`, the universes
of a Stacks site, which is the generality Stacks 03CR is available at; at those universes every
sheafification hypothesis the argument uses is an instance, so none of them is assumed.

**Coherence, 03DL (8), is absent because 03DO does not state it — and could not.**  Stacks 03DL
defines eight local conditions and Stacks 03DM shows all eight are intrinsic, but Stacks 03DO
lists only seven clauses, (1) locally free, (2) finite locally free, (3) locally generated by
sections, (4) locally generated by `r` sections, (5) finite type, (6) quasi-coherent and
(7) finite presentation.  Coherence is deliberately not among them, and the omission is forced:
take for `C` and `D` the punctual site, for `f` the identity morphism of topoi and for `f♯` a
ring map `A ⟶ B`.  Then `f^*` is `- ⊗_A B`, and `SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite` of the unit
module says exactly that the ring is coherent, since the sheaf of relations among `n` sections
over the single object is the kernel of `R^n ⟶ R`.  So with `A` Noetherian and `B` a
non-coherent ring the pullback of the coherent module `O_D` is the non-coherent module `O_C`.

This is why the removal of `[G.Full] [G.Faithful]` from
`Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isCoherentOnSite_iff`, which put 03DM's coherence clause at
exactly the generality its seven siblings enjoy, does not yield an eighth clause here.  That
lemma is the two *vertical* sides of 03CR's square, and coherence does travel along them; what
no hypothesis on those sides can repair is the *bottom* side, the pullback along a morphism
presented by a left exact morphism of sites, where the counterexample above already lives.  The
coherent analogue of the four `_of_twoSided` lemmas below is therefore not merely unproved but
false, and nothing in this file should be tagged `stacks 03DO` for it.  What *is* available for
coherence is the one-sided factorization of an *equivalence*, the addendum to Stacks 03CR, whose
middle arrow is a change of coefficient rings on a single replacement site rather than a morphism
of sites; that argument is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isCoherentOnSite_pullbackModules` in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.CoherentPullbackUnderEquivalence`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03CR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03CR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03D6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03D6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03D8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03D8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DO)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPushforward

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom

universe w

variable {X Y : RingedTopos.{w, w, w}}

/-! ### Lifting a sheaf of modules across a dense subsite inclusion -/

section Lift

variable (a : X.C ⥤ Y.C) [a.IsDenseSubsite X.J Y.J]
  (φ : Y.O ⟶ (pushforwardCommRingFunctor
    (Functor.IsDenseSubsite.morphismOfTopoi X.J Y.J a)).obj X.O)
  [IsIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).fSharpInverseImage]
  (F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))

/-- **The scalars of a sheaf of modules on a dense subsite, restricted along the two inverse
isomorphisms** of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesIsoModuleRestriction`: a sheaf
of modules over the restriction of the ambient structure sheaf along the inclusion.  It is kept
reducible, so that the module it is the restriction of modules of can be read off by
unification. -/
noncomputable abbrev denseSubsiteRestrictScalars :=
  (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars
      (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).inv).obj
    ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars
        (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).hom).obj F)

/-- **A sheaf of modules on a dense subsite is the pullback of one on the ambient site.**  This
is that module: the two restrictions of scalars of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesIsoModuleRestriction` are undone by restricting
along the inverse isomorphisms, and the restriction of modules along the inclusion, which is an
equivalence by the Comparison Lemma, is undone by its quasi-inverse. -/
noncomputable def denseSubsiteLift :
    SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) :=
  (Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestriction X.J Y.J a
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).objPreimage (denseSubsiteRestrictScalars a φ F)

/-- **The pullback of the lift is the module one started from.**  The four steps are
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesIsoModuleRestriction`, the identification of
the restriction of the lift with the module the lift was taken of, and the two cancellations of
a restriction of scalars against the restriction of scalars along the inverse isomorphism. -/
noncomputable def pullbackModulesObjDenseSubsiteLiftIso :
    (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj (denseSubsiteLift a φ F) ≅ F :=
  (pullbackModulesIsoModuleRestriction a φ).app (denseSubsiteLift a φ F) ≪≫
    (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars
          (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).hom ⋙
        SheafOfModules.restrictScalars
          (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).inv).mapIso
      ((Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestriction X.J Y.J a
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).objObjPreimageIso
        (denseSubsiteRestrictScalars a φ F)) ≪≫
    (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars
        (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).inv).mapIso
      ((Stacks.Sheaves.RingedPoint.sheafRestrictScalarsCompIsoId
        (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).inv
        (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).hom
        (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).hom_inv_id).app
        ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars
            (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).hom).obj F)) ≪≫
    (Stacks.Sheaves.RingedPoint.sheafRestrictScalarsCompIsoId
      (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).hom
      (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).inv
      (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).inv_hom_id).app F

variable [a.IsCocontinuous X.J Y.J]

/-- **The lift of a locally free sheaf of modules is locally free.**  This is the clause
03DL (1) travelling across the two restrictions of scalars and then across Stacks 03DM. -/
theorem isLocallyFreeOnSite_denseSubsiteLift (hF : F.IsLocallyFreeOnSite) :
    (denseSubsiteLift a φ F).IsLocallyFreeOnSite := by
  refine (Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isLocallyFreeOnSite_iff X.J Y.J a
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) (denseSubsiteLift a φ F)).2 ?_
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.Intrinsic.isLocallyFreeOnSite_of_iso
    ((Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestriction X.J Y.J a
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).objObjPreimageIso
      (denseSubsiteRestrictScalars a φ F)).symm
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyFreeOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
      (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).inv _
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyFreeOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
        (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).hom F hF))

/-- **The lift of a finite locally free sheaf of modules is finite locally free.**  This is the
clause 03DL (2) travelling across the two restrictions of scalars and then across
Stacks 03DM. -/
theorem isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_denseSubsiteLift (hF : F.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite) :
    (denseSubsiteLift a φ F).IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite := by
  refine (Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_iff X.J Y.J a
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) (denseSubsiteLift a φ F)).2 ?_
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.Intrinsic.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_of_iso
    ((Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestriction X.J Y.J a
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).objObjPreimageIso
      (denseSubsiteRestrictScalars a φ F)).symm
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
      (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).inv _
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
        (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).hom F hF))

/-- **The lift of a sheaf of modules locally generated by sections is locally generated by
sections.**  This is the clause 03DL (3) travelling across the two restrictions of scalars and
then across Stacks 03DM. -/
theorem isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_denseSubsiteLift
    (hF : F.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite) :
    (denseSubsiteLift a φ F).IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite := by
  refine (Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff.{w, w, w}
    X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) (denseSubsiteLift a φ F)).2
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Intrinsic.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_of_iso.{w, w, w}
      ((Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestriction X.J Y.J a
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).objObjPreimageIso
      (denseSubsiteRestrictScalars a φ F)).symm ?_)
  exact (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
      (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).inv _
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
        (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).hom F hF))

/-- **The lift of a quasi-coherent sheaf of modules is quasi-coherent.**  This is the clause
03DL (6) travelling across the two restrictions of scalars and then across Stacks 03DM. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_denseSubsiteLift (hF : F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    (denseSubsiteLift a φ F).IsQuasicoherentOnSite := by
  refine (Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isQuasicoherentOnSite_iff X.J Y.J a
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) (denseSubsiteLift a φ F)).2 ?_
  exact SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite.of_iso
    ((Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestriction X.J Y.J a
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).objObjPreimageIso
      (denseSubsiteRestrictScalars a φ F)).symm
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
      (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).inv _
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
        (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).hom F hF))


/-- **The lift of a coherent sheaf of modules is coherent.**  This is the clause 03DL (8)
travelling across the two restrictions of scalars and then across Stacks 03DM. -/
theorem isCoherentOnSite_denseSubsiteLift (hF : F.IsCoherentOnSite) :
    (denseSubsiteLift a φ F).IsCoherentOnSite := by
  refine (Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isCoherentOnSite_iff X.J Y.J a
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) (denseSubsiteLift a φ F)).2 ?_
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherentOnSite_of_iso
    ((Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestriction X.J Y.J a
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).objObjPreimageIso
      (denseSubsiteRestrictScalars a φ F)).symm
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherentOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
      (restrictionRingIso X.J Y.J a (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)).inv _
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherentOnSite_restrictScalars_of_isIso
        (asIso (ofDenseSubsite a φ).toModulesHom.fSharpInverseImage).hom F hF))

end Lift

/-! ### The clauses carried around the square of Stacks 03CR -/

section Square

/-- The inverse image of `f♯` for a dense subsite inclusion is invertible when `φ` is. -/
private theorem isIso_fSharpInverseImage_ofDenseSubsite {X Y : RingedTopos.{w, w, w}}
    (a : X.C ⥤ Y.C) [a.IsDenseSubsite X.J Y.J]
    (φ : Y.O ⟶ (pushforwardCommRingFunctor
      (Functor.IsDenseSubsite.morphismOfTopoi X.J Y.J a)).obj X.O) (hφ : IsIso φ) :
    IsIso (ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := Y) a φ).fSharpInverseImage := by
  have : (ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := Y) a φ).toToposHom.pushforward.IsEquivalence :=
    Functor.IsDenseSubsite.morphismOfTopoi_pushforward_isEquivalence X.J Y.J a
  have : IsIso (ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := Y) a φ).fSharp := inferInstanceAs (IsIso φ)
  exact isIso_fSharpInverseImage (ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := Y) a φ)

variable (f : RingedToposHom X Y) {X' Y' : RingedTopos.{w, w, w}}
  {a : X.C ⥤ X'.C} [a.IsDenseSubsite X.J X'.J]
  {b : Y.C ⥤ Y'.C} [b.IsDenseSubsite Y.J Y'.J]
  (φ : X'.O ⟶ (pushforwardCommRingFunctor
    (Functor.IsDenseSubsite.morphismOfTopoi X.J X'.J a)).obj X.O) (hφ : IsIso φ)
  (ψ : Y'.O ⟶ (pushforwardCommRingFunctor
    (Functor.IsDenseSubsite.morphismOfTopoi Y.J Y'.J b)).obj Y.O) (hψ : IsIso ψ)
  {c : Y'.C ⥤ X'.C} [HasFiniteLimits Y'.C] [PreservesFiniteLimits c]
  (hc : c.IsMorphismOfSites Y'.J X'.J)
  (h : RingedToposHom X' Y') (hh : h.toToposHom = hc.morphismOfTopoi)
  (t : (RingedToposHom.comp (X := X) (Y := X') (Z := Y') h
      (ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := X') a φ)).TwoIso
    (RingedToposHom.comp (X := X) (Y := Y) (Z := Y')
      (ofDenseSubsite (X := Y) (Y := Y') b ψ) f))
  (F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))

/-- **The identification `g^*(h^*G) ≅ f^*F` attached to the square of Stacks 03CR**, where `G`
is the lift of `F` across the right-hand vertical arrow.  The two composites are split by the
pseudo-functoriality of Stacks 03D8 and identified by the 2-isomorphism, and the lift is
identified with `F` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesObjDenseSubsiteLiftIso`. -/
noncomputable def twoSidedSquareIso
    [IsIso (ofDenseSubsite (X := Y) (Y := Y') b ψ).fSharpInverseImage] :
    (ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := X') a φ).toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj
        (h.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj (denseSubsiteLift b ψ F)) ≅
      f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F :=
  ((pullbackModulesCompIso (ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := X') a φ) h).app
      (denseSubsiteLift b ψ F)).symm ≪≫
    t.pullbackModulesIso.app (denseSubsiteLift b ψ F) ≪≫
    (pullbackModulesCompIso f (ofDenseSubsite (X := Y) (Y := Y') b ψ)).app
      (denseSubsiteLift b ψ F) ≪≫
    f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.mapIso (pullbackModulesObjDenseSubsiteLiftIso b ψ F)

include hφ hψ hh t in
/-- **Local freeness travels around the square of Stacks 03CR.** -/
theorem isLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules_of_twoSided (hF : F.IsLocallyFreeOnSite) :
    (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F).IsLocallyFreeOnSite := by
  have := isIso_fSharpInverseImage_ofDenseSubsite a φ hφ
  have := isIso_fSharpInverseImage_ofDenseSubsite b ψ hψ
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.Intrinsic.isLocallyFreeOnSite_of_iso
    (twoSidedSquareIso f φ ψ h t F)
    (isLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules_ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := X') a φ _
      (isLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules_of_isMorphismOfSites h hc hh _
        (isLocallyFreeOnSite_denseSubsiteLift b ψ F hF)))

include hφ hψ hh t in
/-- **Finite local freeness travels around the square of Stacks 03CR.** -/
theorem isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules_of_twoSided
    (hF : F.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite) :
    (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F).IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite := by
  have := isIso_fSharpInverseImage_ofDenseSubsite a φ hφ
  have := isIso_fSharpInverseImage_ofDenseSubsite b ψ hψ
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.Intrinsic.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_of_iso
    (twoSidedSquareIso f φ ψ h t F)
    (isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules_ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := X') a φ _
      (isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules_of_isMorphismOfSites h hc hh _
        (isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_denseSubsiteLift b ψ F hF)))

include hφ hψ hh t in
/-- **Local generation by sections travels around the square of Stacks 03CR.** -/
theorem isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_pullbackModules_of_twoSided
    (hF : F.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite) :
    (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F).IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite := by
  have := isIso_fSharpInverseImage_ofDenseSubsite a φ hφ
  have := isIso_fSharpInverseImage_ofDenseSubsite b ψ hψ
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.Intrinsic.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_of_iso.{w, w, w}
    (twoSidedSquareIso f φ ψ h t F)
    (isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_pullbackModules_ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := X') a φ _
      (isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_pullbackModules_of_isMorphismOfSites h hc hh _
        (isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_denseSubsiteLift b ψ F hF)))

include hφ hψ hh t in
/-- **Quasi-coherence travels around the square of Stacks 03CR.** -/
theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_pullbackModules_of_twoSided (hF : F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F).IsQuasicoherentOnSite := by
  have := isIso_fSharpInverseImage_ofDenseSubsite a φ hφ
  have := isIso_fSharpInverseImage_ofDenseSubsite b ψ hψ
  exact SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite.of_iso
    (twoSidedSquareIso f φ ψ h t F)
    (isQuasicoherentOnSite_pullbackModules_ofDenseSubsite (X := X) (Y := X') a φ _
      (isQuasicoherentOnSite_pullbackModules_of_isMorphismOfSites h hc hh _
        (isQuasicoherentOnSite_denseSubsiteLift b ψ F hF)))

end Square

/-! ### Stacks 03DO for an arbitrary morphism of ringed topoi -/

section General

variable (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
  (F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))

/-- **Stacks 03DO for the clause 03DL (1).**  If a sheaf of `O_D`-modules is locally free, then
so is its pullback along an arbitrary morphism of ringed topoi
`(f, f♯) : (Sh(C), O_C) ⟶ (Sh(D), O_D)`.

